    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92333" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥήν</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sheep, lamb</i> (not found in
			nom.), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥήνεσσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.1497
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥῆνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					453
				</span></i>
			. (From <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ϝρήν</span>, old nom. of
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ϝάρνα, ϝαρνός</span>, etc., 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρήν</span>
			, and cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολύ-ρρην</span>:—also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥᾶνα:
				ἄρνα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> (perh. Elean); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρανόν</span> [i.e.
			perh. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ϝρᾶνον]: ἑξαμηνιαῖον
			πρόβατον</span>, Id.)</div>
